{"_id":"6a2ff9b02204ffbc59e5a7b3","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"GRg7HyeVuSwkKD5bCOFiY","description":"# Subplots and figures\n\nMatplotlib's `Figure` is the top-level container, and `Axes` objects are the individual plots within it. `plt.subplots(rows, cols)` creates a grid of axes for displaying multiple plots side by side. Subplots are used to compare distributions across groups or to show multiple related variables in one figure.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Create multiple subplots using plt.subplots","url":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/gallery/subplots_axes_and_figures/subplots_demo.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeba7"},{"type":"article","title":"Matplotlib: Part 4. Subplots, Layouts, and Advanced Customizations","url":"https://medium.com/@ebimsv/mastering-matplotlib-part-4-subplots-layouts-and-advanced-customizations-2f07c4a99e80","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeba8"},{"type":"article","title":"Introduction to Multi-figure Layouts","url":"https://codesignal.com/learn/courses/customizing-and-styling-plots/lessons/multi-figure-layouts-with-matplotlib","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeba9"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:10:08.709Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/GRg7HyeVuSwkKD5bCOFiY.md"}